<Project>
  <!-- IAP-015 Option-B split-proof harness (t_0d853e78).

       Deliberately does NOT import the repo-root Directory.Build.props. MSBuild
       walks up and stops at the FIRST Directory.Build.props it finds, so this
       file shields the harness from the root's SbprValidateSdkPaths target (which
       hard-errors unless the Valheim managed-assembly path is set).

       CRITICAL DIFFERENCE from tests/ and qa-operator-harness/: this harness does
       NOT link-compile shipped source. It takes a BINARY <Reference> on the
       COMPILED candidate product assembly (SBPR.Niflheim.HomesteadStones.dll) and
       attests its SHA-256 at runtime before exercising it. The proven behaviour is
       therefore the SHIPPED, COMPILED behaviour of the exact candidate binary — not
       a source-linked test double or a reimplementation. See README.md. -->
</Project>
